                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "何\n\nOk to be serious let's really talk about this, maybe the creator will learn something.\n\nFor one, the concept is actually pretty interesting. Every player has the same player model and you're in a room filled to the brim with your player model. It's like a hybrid hide and seek/shooter, and for that, I can give it credit.\n\nEverything else is objectively trash. There's a huge difference between where you're aiming and where your bullet goes. The graphics are lackluster and the controls are basically just the prebuilt Unity third person controls with a little bit of modification. More maps and game modes would help, but that wouldn't help the fact that no one is playing this game, probably for two reasons: No one owns this \"gem\", and no one wants to put up with the horrendous matchmaking that you can't even back out of without quitting the game.\n\nA more fitting name is Wasted Potential.",
